#: src/Admin/Settings.php:191
msgid "Withdrawal period (days)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:193
msgid ""
"Statutory minimum is 14 days from the day the customer receives the goods. "
"For services and digital content it is 14 days from the day the contract is "
"concluded, so an order of only virtual products counts from the day it was "
"placed. The order has no delivery date, so for goods the plugin counts from "
"the day the order is marked completed (or created, if it never was); a "
"shipping plugin can supply the real date through the withdraw/delivery_date "
"filter. The start day is not counted, the period ends at midnight of its "
"last day, and a last day on a Saturday or Sunday moves to the Monday "
"(Regulation 1182/71, Art. 3)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:196
msgid "Extra days (grace)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:198
msgid ""
"Days added after the statutory period ends, for example to cover shipping "
"time when orders are completed at dispatch rather than at delivery."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:203
msgid "Refuse the declaration"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:204
msgid "Accept it and flag it as late"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:206
msgid ""
"A withdrawal counts as in time if the customer sent it before the period "
"expired (Directive 2011/83/EU, Art. 11a(5)), and for goods the period runs "
"from delivery (Art. 9(2)(b)). If your completion date can be earlier than "
"delivery, accept late declarations and judge each one against the real "
"delivery date. Links in My Account and in emails still disappear at the "
"deadline."
msgstr ""

